@startuml
' Sem skinparam aqui: a paleta e injetada por tools/render-puml.py
' para gerar as variantes light e dark a partir desta mesma fonte.

participant "Scheduler" as SCH
participant "Dispatcher" as DIS
participant "YouTube API" as YT
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
queue "Redis Streams" as RS
participant "Sentiment\nXLM-RoBERTa (local)" as SENT
participant "NLP\nspaCy (local)" as NLP
participant "Utterance cycle\ndistiluse 512d (local)" as UTT
participant "Narrative cycle\nclustering" as NAR
participant "Cost cap" as CAP
participant "Claude Haiku 4.5" as LLM

== Collection ==
SCH -> DIS : tick every 300s
DIS -> YT : commentThreads.list
DIS -> DB : publication and reaction stored separately\nauthor identity salted-hashed
DIS -> RS : publish mention.captured

== Local classification ==
RS -> SENT : consume
SENT -> DB : sentiment label + intensity\nbelow threshold, flag for human review
RS -> NLP : consume
NLP -> DB : entities, source region and text region\nnever merged — no guessing below 0.5

== Interpretation ==
UTT -> DB : speech type by calibrated rules\n(claim, support, mockery, question, noise)
note right of UTT
  Nothing is discarded. Noise becomes a row —
  so the sample can be reported honestly as
  "1,200 utterances, 300 of them noise"
end note
UTT -> DB : 512-dimension meaning vector per utterance

== Narrative clustering ==
NAR -> DB : read window of claims
NAR -> NAR : agglomerate at 0.60 similarity\ncalibrated on 24,090 real comment pairs
alt matches an existing cluster
  NAR -> DB : attach evidence, update centroid
else new cluster with 3+ evidences
  NAR -> CAP : guard(operator)
  alt cap reached
    CAP --> NAR : skip — no call made
  else within budget
    NAR -> LLM : forced tool call — name this cluster
    LLM --> NAR : tool_use block\n(free-form answer is an error, not a fallback)
    NAR -> DB : persist named narrative
  end
else new cluster with fewer evidences
  NAR -> DB : stays emergent — no label, no screen
end
NAR -> RS : publish narrative.updated

note over NAR, LLM
  The model reads GROUPS, never individual comments.
  A subject with 5,000 utterances costs 6 to 10 calls, not 5,000.
end note

@enduml
